@startuml client_connection_send_wait_reply_activity
title ClientConnection - sending and waiting for a reply

start
:SendWaitReply(message, reply);
if (IsInCallback()?) then (yes)
    :Return EAGAIN without blocking the engine callback thread;
    stop
else (no)
    :Call is outside engine callback context;
endif
if (message.size() > max_send_size_?) then (yes)
    :Return EMSGSIZE;
    stop
else (no)
    :Message size is admissible;
endif
if (state_ != kReady?) then (yes)
    :Return EINVAL;
    stop
else (no)
    :Connection is ready at the admission check;
endif

:Prepare result and NonAllocatingFuture(send_mutex_, send_condition_, result);
:Create completion callback capturing reply and future by reference;
note right
    Completion callback:
    On error, store that error and mark the result ready.
    If the received reply exceeds reply.size(), store EMSGSIZE.
    Otherwise copy bytes into the caller's reply buffer and store
    a span trimmed to the received size. Mark the result ready.
    Marking ready notifies send_condition_.
end note

:Lock send_mutex_;
if (waiting_for_reply_ is engaged?) then (yes)
    :TryQueueMessage(message, move(completion callback));
    if (Message admitted to send_queue_?) then (yes)
        :Leave the existing reply/drain slot in place;
    else (no)
        :Unlock send_mutex_;
        :Return ENOBUFS: no free send command;
        stop
    endif
else (no)
    :Move completion callback into waiting_for_reply_;
    :Unlock send_mutex_;
    :SendProtocolMessage(client_fd_, REQUEST, message);
    :Relock send_mutex_;
    if (Transport failed?) then (yes)
        if (send_queue_ is empty?) then (yes)
            :Reset waiting_for_reply_;
        else (no)
            :ArmSendQueueUnderLock();
            note right
                This is the existing direct-error recovery call.
                Its reply-slot precondition is a queue-design review gap.
            end note
        endif
        :Unlock send_mutex_;
        :Return the transport error without waiting for completion;
        stop
    else (no)
        :Request was sent successfully;
    endif
endif

:Unlock send_mutex_;
:future.Wait(): wait until the completion callback has marked the result ready;
note right
    The predicate also handles completion before Wait() begins.
    The condition wait releases send_mutex_ while blocked.
    No reply deadline is applied by this method.
end note
:Return the reply span or completion error;
stop

legend
    A free reply/drain slot causes direct transport regardless
    of fully_ordered or truly_async. An engaged slot causes queuing.
    During direct transport the occupied slot makes other request
    callers queue, while send_mutex_ is released.
    The local future and referenced reply buffer remain in scope
    until completion, except on immediate admission/transport failure.
    Queue dispatch and reply delivery are separate continuations.
endlegend

@enduml